2) ONNX Runtime (submodule, required runtime)
    - Project: https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime
    - Path: external/onnxruntime (Git submodule)
    - License: MIT License
    - Notes: Built from source for Android (CPU execution provider, Java bindings) via
      scripts/build_onnxruntime_android.sh. The resulting native libraries and
      Java JAR are integrated into app/jniLibs and app/libs respectively as part
      of the required ONNX Runtime support. The MIT license text is included at
      third_party_licenses/onnxruntime_LICENSE.txt.
    - Pinned build files (external/onnxruntime_pinned/):
      Three Gradle build files from the upstream ONNX Runtime repository
      (java/build-android.gradle, java/settings-android.gradle,
      java/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties) have been copied and
      modified to enable building the Android AAR with JDK 21 and to keep
      versions aligned with the Make a Copy host project. The following
      changes were made compared to the upstream originals:
        * build-android.gradle:
          – Android Gradle Plugin updated from 7.4.2 to 8.12.0 (kept in sync
            with makeacopy gradle/libs.versions.toml).
          – compileSdkVersion raised from 34 to 36 (kept in sync with
            makeacopy app/build.gradle).
          – Nested `android { lintOptions }` block flattened to top-level
            `lintOptions` inside the `android` block.
          – Removed upstream code comments (QNN format notes, version-code
            format documentation, artifact-id comment, publish-repo comment,
            AAR header-packaging comment).
          – Reformatted indentation from tabs to spaces for consistency.
          – `task.doLast` closure in `whenTaskAdded` wrapped correctly to
            reference `task.archivePath`.
          – Added sync-marker comments referencing makeacopy configuration.
        * settings-android.gradle:
          – Added `pluginManagement` block with google(), mavenCentral(), and
            gradlePluginPortal() repositories (required by AGP 8.x).
          – Added sync-marker comment referencing makeacopy AGP version.
        * gradle-wrapper.properties:
          – Gradle distribution updated from 8.7 to 8.13 (kept in sync with
            makeacopy gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties).
          – SHA-256 checksum updated accordingly.
          – Added sync-marker comment referencing makeacopy wrapper.


10) Training Datasets (not redistributed)

This project uses ideas and publicly available datasets for training and
evaluation purposes only. No datasets, images, labels, or training
checkpoints/weights are included or redistributed in this repository.

The following datasets were used:

10.1) UVDoc Dataset
     - Project: https://github.com/tanguymagne/UVDoc-Dataset
     - License: MIT License
     - Reference: Floor Verhoeven et al., "Neural Grid-based Document Unwarping"
       (SIGGRAPH Asia 2023)
     - Usage: Pretraining of document geometry and perspective.

10.2) SmartDoc Dataset
     - Reference: Jean-Christophe Burie et al.,
       "ICDAR 2015 Competition on Smartphone Document Capture and OCR (SmartDoc)"
     - License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
       https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
     - Usage: Finetuning and robustness training on real smartphone document images.
     - Notes: Original images remain the property of their respective authors.
       Attribution is provided here as required by the CC BY 4.0 license.

10.3) Describable Textures Dataset (DTD)

     - Project: https://www.robots.ox.ac.uk/~vgg/data/dtd/
     - Reference: M. Cimpoi et al., "Describing Textures in the Wild"
       (CVPR 2014)
     - License: No explicit license text is included in the original
       dataset distribution.
     - Usage: Used exclusively during internal training for background
       diversification and robustness experiments (background replacement).
     - Notes: The dataset and any images derived from it are not included
       or redistributed as part of this repository or application.
       This project does not ship any DTD images or derivatives.

10.4) CORD Dataset (Consolidated Receipt Dataset)
     - Project: https://github.com/clovaai/cord
     - Reference: Jaewook Kim et al.,
       "CORD: A Consolidated Receipt Dataset for Post-OCR Parsing"
       (ICDAR 2019)
     - License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
       https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
     - Usage: Finetuning and evaluation for receipt-specific document geometry
       and robustness.
     - Notes: Original images and annotations remain the property of their
       respective authors. Attribution is provided here as required by the
       CC BY 4.0 license. No CORD images, annotations, or derivatives are
       redistributed with this project.


